c('THM-LATTICE-FINITE-CERTIFICATES','moment','For mu_m=m(m−1), a_m=mu_m²W_m>=0 and nu=sum a_m delta_mu_m, R_M=int product_(j=2)^M(x−mu_j)dnu gives sum_(m>M)a_m<=R_M/D_M, D_M=(M−1)!(2M)!/(M+1)!. Zero residual forces support<=M. Signed Lagrange mass enclosures and nearest-lattice quadratic witnesses have exact rational constants.','Finite supplied moments of a feasible positive lattice measure; all derivative data are true limiting coefficients, not finite-N staircases. M=1 uses the empty product.','exact_positive_measure_certificates')
c('THM-LATTICE-AUGMENTED-FEASIBILITY','moment','For y0>0 and n>=1 the normalized data (moments through n, C0/y0) are feasible iff they lie in conv{(x,...,x^n,g(x)):x=m(m−1),m>=2} plus the nonnegative vertical ray; g(x)=4/(sqrt(1+4x)−1)^2. Feasible boundary data have a unique finite profile with <=n+1 support points; interior profiles can occupy every lattice point.','C0 constraint includes W1=C0−int g dnu>=0; finite exact moment data, true algebraic convex hull, not its closure.','exact_augmented_moment_classification')
c('OBS-LATTICE-MOMENT-ESCAPE','moment','The data (y0,y1,y2,C0)=(1,6,37,1/4) are infeasible but lie in the closure of feasible data. For x=m(m−1), m>=4, weights at2,6,x given by 1/[4(x−2)],1−w2−wx,1/[(x−6)(x−2)] preserve the three pure moments while g-cost decreases to1/4 and remote second moment tends to1.','Synthetic positive lattice measures; exact Jensen obstruction; no counterexample to an arithmetic RH prefix formula.','exact_nonclosedness_countermodel')
c('CERT-LATTICE-RATIONAL-CLI','moment','The Fraction-based CLI produces rigorous rational/interval tail and atom enclosures conditional on a feasible positive profile, and explicitly returns feasibility_checked:false. Independent controls include 540 feasible profiles, malformed input, infeasibility-scope cases and exact repeated examples.','Experiments/code/prefix_moment63_certificates.py and its documented schema; no full moment-feasibility decision asserted.','reviewed_exact_computation')
c('THM-JUMP-GENERATOR-DOMAIN','group','On S=ell²(1/[n(n+1)]), G=i(D−H), Db_n=log n b_n, Hb_n=sum_(r<n)log(1+1/r)b_r, with DomG={sum w_n log²n |b_n|²<infinity}; finite cells form a graph core and MGb=−i[(Mb)prime+(Mb)/s].','Exact jump-phase group, strong derivative in S; H bounded with norm<=2.','closed_operator_reconstruction','PAPER-MN2026-VERTICAL')
c('THM-JUMP-RESOLVENT-SPECTRUM','group','For q_n=(lambda−i log n)^−1, (lambda−G)^−1=diag q−iH diag(q_n q_(n+1)); it is compact, spectrum={i log n}, each algebraically simple. Projection P_n b=(b_n−b_(n−1))1_[n,infinity) has norm sqrt(2n); resolvent singular values are asymptotic1/log j and belong to no finite Schatten class.','The same weighted S and closed domain; lambda outside the displayed discrete set. This spectrum is indexed by integers, not zeta zeros.','operator_spectral_reconstruction')
c('THM-JUMP-INVARIANT-METRICS','group','Every bounded positive invariant form is sum d_n|b_n−b_(n−1)|² with d_n>=0 and sup n²d_n finite. It is injective iff every d_n>0 and is never coercive; no bounded invertible metric unitarizes the group.','Invariance under all real times on the original S; a weaker completion changes topology.','positive_metric_classification')
c('THM-JUMP-FLOW-SUBSPACES','group','Every closed forward-flow invariant subspace is exactly a closed span of selected integer eigenvectors 1_[n,infinity). Every vector with all jumps nonzero is forward-orbit cyclic.','All times t>=0, Laplace resolvent analyticity and convergent subsequence of natural spectral sums; a single fixed-time criterion is separate.','invariant_subspace_classification')
c('OBS-JUMP-EXACT-ANTECEDENT','group','The source jump group is exactly the time-reversed adjoint of the logarithmic multiplier group in Sklyar–Marchenko, under the unitary first-difference realization. Prior resolvent and nonbasis results apply to the same operator family.','Pinned arXiv1405.2731v4 and current source conventions; old version-only clauses are distinguished.','exact_primary_source_intertwining','PAPER-SM2017-LOGGROUP')
c('THM-SHIFT-RUNLENGTH-BASIS','basis','For k>=1, phi_n=(I−T)^k e_n from a Riesz basis with associated shift, a selected sequence is Riesz iff its consecutive index runs are uniformly bounded. For run bound r, squared bounds are A[2−2cos(pi/(r+1))]^k and B4^k. Unbounded runs preclude a Schauder basis in every ordering.','Ordinary one-sided shift and fixed k; explicit normalized polynomial witnesses establish the negative direction.','replacement_basis_theorem')
c('OBS-SKLYAR-SUPERSEDED-CLAUSES','basis','The v1 domain restriction and v1–v3 blanket no-subsequence-basis clause are superseded. Sparse block-separated difference vectors give Riesz subsequences; v4 omits the latter clause. No inaccessible journal-text error is inferred.','Source versions explicitly compared; journal text unavailable in inspected routes.','historical_version_counterexample_and_correction','PAPER-SM2017-LOGGROUP')
c('THM-GENERATOR-ONE-MEMBER-RH','member','For every fixed integer k>=2, RH iff G f_k belongs to W, where f_k=k floor(x/k)−floor x and W is the closed NB span. MGf_k=−i[ zeta(s)(k^(1−s)−1)]prime/s; a right-zero derivative jet gives an explicit positive off-RH distance.','Closed domain verified for f_k; full multiplicity jet, fixed k; forward uses classical density. Balazard holomorphy/jump-series antecedents are credited.','fixed_target_equivalent_criterion')
c('THM-GENERATOR-CHARACTER-CRITERIA','member','For fixed nonprincipal chi, GRH_chi iff G S_chi is in the unrestricted dilation closure. For principal chi use anchored g_chi,k=S_chi(x/k)−S_chi(x)/k; membership Gg in its anchored span is equivalent to RH. For nonprincipal chi the same anchored Gg is never a member since its Mellin value at1 is iL(1,chi)log k/k.','Fixed character, ordinary integer dilations, classical nonvanishing at1; principal raw summatory function is outside S.','fixed_character_criterion_and_anchor_obstruction')
c('THM-CHARACTER-EULER-SPAN-EQUALITY','member','Deleting finitely many Euler factors preserves the unrestricted nonprincipal dilation span and preserves both principal/nonprincipal anchored spans unconditionally. Finite Euler dilation factors have bounded Neumann inverses; [G,U_d]=i log d U_d transfers exact generator membership.','Fixed modulus and finite factors, norm U_d=d^−1/2; no conductor-uniform assertion.','unconditional_span_identity')
c('THM-RST048-FINITE-EXCEPTIONS','foz','Under finitely many right off-line nontrivial zeta zeros, V is exactly the joint Mellin-jet kernel in the unit-step space. With u=P_V(1/s), d_N² tends to D_infinity² and logN(d_N²−D_infinity²) tends to sum_critical_distinct m_rho²|u(rho)|². The unrestricted analogue uses u_star and the separately minimized pole scalar and has the same target-value rule.','Fixed finite exceptional configuration including multiplicities; discrete projection targets, not continuous Blaschke products; source integer quadrature and fixed Laurent repair retained. No extra factor1/|rho|².','conditional_source_theorem_reconstruction','PAPER-RST048')
c('THM-TAPERED-PRIME-ARRAY','array','For each fixed k>=2, w_k(d)=k1_(k|d)Lambda(d/k)−Lambda(d)+k logk1_(d=k), A_N=sum_(d<=N)w_k(d)(1−logd/logN)d^−s and B_N=A_N−A_N(1). Under RH, logN||MR_k−zeta B_N/s||² tends to C_k=sum_simple_critical |zetaprime(rho)(k^(1−rho)−1)|²/|rho|². The best anchored and unrestricted ordinary polynomials have the same leading constant.','R_k,n=log[(floor(n/k)!)^k k^(k floor(n/k))/n!]; fixed k, full dt/(2pi) norm; multiple zeros contribute0; no simplicity or inverse derivative moment.','prescribed_array_asymptotic')
c('THM-TAPERED-PRIME-ARRAY-RH-IFF','array','For every fixed k>=2, convergence to zero of the prescribed tapered anchored prime-array error is equivalent to RH. Fixed finite complex target combinations have the polarized quadratic limit under RH.','Forward requires RH; converse uses a fixed right-zero jet and no bound on polynomial coefficients; no target index growing with N in the leading constant statement.','equivalent_criterion_with_prescribed_coefficients')
c('THM-PRIME-ARRAY-EFFECTIVE','effective','Under RH, every integer N>=3 has E_N(2)<=10^27/logN and E_N(k)<=10^44 k^6/logN for every integer k>=2.','E_N is the full squared anchored error of the explicit array. Coarse global constants, not optimized or practical thresholds; no simplicity assumption.','effective_global_conditional_bounds')
c('COR-PRIME-ARRAY-MOVING-INDEX','effective','For any prescribed integer sequence k_N>=2 with k_N^6/logN tending to0, E_N(k_N) tends to0 iff RH.','Uniform effective upper and fixed off-line-zero jet lower; no joint leading-constant or inverse-recovery rate claimed.','derived_moving_index_equivalence')
c('CERT-PRIME-ARRAY-FINITE-NORMS','effective','Unconditional full squared errors at k=2,N=10,30,100 lie respectively in [0.342801539918328691,0.343111054662620134], [0.247656566621497315,0.247904631616511935], [0.179598089981701525,0.179908683595524940].','Original160/224-bit Arb runs with infinite tail bounds, pinned v1 and independent replay; hardened v2 separately recorded. No numerical limit inference.','validated_finite_norm_certificates')
c('OBS-HARD-MANGOLDT-DIVERGENCE','effective','A_kM=log k(f_k−f_M)+sum_(d<=M)Lambda(d) f_k(x/d) matches R_k for x<M but ||R_k−A_kM||²>=M(logk)²/68 and is Theta_k(M).','This exact renormalized anchored hard cutoff, fixed k>=2; elementary binomial/Legendre bounds, no PNT. Not every hard cutoff.','unconditional_negative_approximation_theorem')
c('THM-PRIME-FORM-FOURIER-INVERSE','inverse','Under RH, all fixed-target limiting real quadratic forms determine the finite symmetric simple-zero measure nu=sum |zetaprime(rho)|²/|rho|² delta_gamma. C_k=(k+1)B−2sqrt(k)F(logk), B=lim C_k/k, and difference forms recover F(log(k/l)).','Exact limiting data, finiteness and symmetry; arithmetic N limit first. Multiple zeros and derivative phases are invisible.','conditional_inverse_theorem')
c('THM-PRIME-SINGLETON-ATOM-INVERSE','inverse','Singleton C_k alone recover every atom by logarithmic Cesaro quadrature: nu{x}=lim_(K→infinity)sum_(k=2)^K log(1+1/k)F(logk)e^(ixlogk)/log(K+1). Replacing B with C_K/K in all samples adds O(B/logK).','Finite symmetric measure; whole-measure uniqueness from singleton data holds in the pure atomic class. No uniform finite-data modulus.','atomic_inverse_theorem')
c('OBS-PRIME-INVERSE-FINITE-AMBIGUITY','inverse','Every finite collection of form data admits different positive symmetric atomic measures, even with supplied equal mass; without mass, entire-kernel evaluation at i/2 gives different-mass competitors. All singleton data can miss diffuse measures. o(sqrt k) singleton errors preserve atomic recovery but O(sqrt k) can conceal distinct profiles.','Synthetic positive measures, not alternative zeta functions. Exact finite/noisy data are not full infinite limiting information.','inverse_problem_obstructions')
c('THM-HLZ-FIXED-DERIVATIVE-MOMENT','hlz','For fixed real Dirichlet polynomial Q, RH gives sum_(0<gamma<=T)|zetaprime(rho)Q(rho)|²=S(Q)Tlog^4T/(24pi)+O_Q(Tlog^3T), S=sum a_m a_n/lcm(m,n).','Heap–Li–Zhao journal Thm5 complex-shift uniformity and coefficient hypotheses; arbitrary fixed sparse support handled by divisor-closed positive padding and quadratic identity.','source_dependent_derived_asymptotic','PAPER-DM63-HLZ2022')
c('THM-HLZ-GCD-TAIL','hlz','For fixed k,l, the two-sided derivative-weighted Q_k,Q_l tail is (gcd(k,l)−1)log^4Y/(12piY)+O_(k,l)(log^3Y/Y). For Q=1 the coefficient is1.','RH; Q_k=k^(1−s)−1; strict-tail endpoint and both ordinate signs retained, multiple zeros vanish; no growing-index uniformity in this claim.','derived_arithmetic_tail_asymptotic')
c('THM-PRIME-POISSON-TORUS','hlz','Under RH, normalized high tails of nu pushed to (p^(−i gamma))_p converge weakly on the countable prime torus to independent Poisson circle laws with radii p^−1/2. Factorial variables have mean0 and covariance gcd(k,l)−1=sum_(d|k,d|l,d>=2)phi(d).','Fixed character tests before Y limit; source moment theorem plus partial summation. One weighted ordinate, not spacing or unweighted zero statistics.','cross_paper_harmonic_connection')
c('OBS-PRIME-PHASE-NONUNIFORMITY','hlz','For each fixed positive tail mass B_Y, the supremum over distinct prime pairs of |F_Y(log(p/q))/B_Y−1/sqrt(pq)| is at least1. The fixed-rational limiting coefficient is discontinuous at0 in the ordinary real topology and is not a real-line probability Fourier transform.','Continuity of each finite actual tail Fourier transform and arbitrarily close large prime ratios; compatible with fixed-prime torus convergence.','uniformity_and_topology_obstruction')
c('THM-DENSITY-WEIGHTED-SLABS','density','A fixed positive gap2(1−sigma)−E(sigma)>0 removes each compact slab from the BGSTB positive weighted majorant by a fixed mesh. Palomar right branch3(1−sigma)/(2sigma) removes every compact slab in(3/4,1), but value at3/4 remains9/16; Pintz wins above9/10.','Source density bounds with fixed sigma,epsilon, constants; near1 requires separate uniform external input. These are majorant consequences, not necessary signed-cancellation conditions.','source_dependent_density_synthesis')
c('THM-DENSITY-SINGLE-WINDOW','density','Combining Ye local bounds and an accepted uniform upper-tail input gives weighted o(T) in each comparable-height O(T^b) window for every fixed0<b<13/15. The7/10 layer, not3/4, is critical. No full-block saving follows by covering.','Fixed b, split point v just above3/4, correct source branch join; for b<2/3 use nesting.','sharp_implication_of_density_inputs')
c('OBS-DENSITY-ALL-HEIGHT-ESCAPE','density','One fixed reflected positive multiset can satisfy all inspected global/local density bounds, RVM O(logT), unit counts, proportion lower bounds and off-line o(T), while D_T(1/2)=o(T), r_T→0 locally and M_T/T→2 along all real heights. Separate lacunary7/10 blocks show13/15 sharp for the stated inputs.','Explicit two-curve counting model with critical fillers. Does not impose actual zeta explicit formula, signed pair identity or Dirichlet-sum triggers.','all_height_negative_inference_model')
c('LEM-DENSITY-DYADIC-TIGHTNESS','density','After upper-tail removal, D_T(a)=o(T) and a uniform bound Y^−1 integral_Y^(2Y) r_T(y)dy<=C Y^(1−kappa), kappa>0, imply M_T=o(T).','Exact layer identity, positive counting, uniform constants in Y,T; the displayed sufficient missing arithmetic hypothesis is unproved for actual zeta.','conditional_sufficient_missing_lemma')
c('CERT-PALOMAR-FULL-CURVE-QUERY','density','The actual cached Lean full_curve and uniform_away_boundary declarations compiled/query exited0 with exactly propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound and unchanged pinned module. Quantifiers differ: fixed sigma,epsilon then constants versus fixed delta,epsilon then all sigma,T.','Pinned Palomar source/Lean/mathlib receipts and raw declaration types; not a new build, axiom-free proof, or RH result.','actual_formal_component_query')
c('OBS-MANZUR-COVARIANCE-SIGN','whole','In arXiv2610.03568v1 §6 both displayed covariance phases require n^(−i tau), not n^(i tau). For n=2,tau=pi/(2log2),e0 the printed direct relation says e0+e1=−e0−e1. The main Theorem5.1 and printed operator matrix survive the correction.','Exact pinned seven-page v1, no RH needed for the witness; two independent complete reviews and director reconstruction.','verified_versioned_auxiliary_display_error','PAPER-MN2026-VERTICAL')
c('LEM-MANZUR-RIGHT-SHIFT-EXTENSION','whole','For Re alpha>0, the same Copson-row construction with d_j=(j+1)^−alpha is bounded and satisfies T_alpha* k_s=(bar s+bar alpha)k_(s+alpha)/bar s with nonzero scalar.','Disk Hardy kernels with Re s>1/2; this separately answers the motivating right-shift question, whereas source T_tau is vertical. No novelty claim.','elementary_operator_extension')
c('OBS-LEE-PANKOWSKI-TARGET','lee','The literal new theorem statements omit nonvanishing although both proofs take log f. On D_(1/8)(3/4), f(s)=s−3/4 and epsilon1/16 force a right-strip zero by Rouche, so underRH the good set is empty. Global zero density does not by itself refute the unconditional short-window limsup.','Pinned arxivv1 and journal version; intended zero-free target repair, no public error flag or unconditional main theorem refutation.','missing_hypothesis_with_exact_scope','PAPER-DM63-LEEPANKOWSKI2025')
c('THM-HLZ-UNIFORM-POLYLOG-PHASE','uniform','Under RH, for every fixed D,B>0 and all m,n<=log^D Y, mn T_Y(e_m,e_n)/B_Y=g+O_(D,B)(g log(mn/g²)/logY+log^(−B)Y), g=gcd(m,n). The diagonal is exactlym, and normalized Fourier absolute error is O_D(1/logY).','Two-sided symmetric derivative weights; source-uniform bounded padding before cancellation, exact untwisted normalization and arbitrary log saving. Siegel cutoff ineffective, no numerical onset.','uniform_source_dependent_asymptotic')
c('THM-HLZ-GROWING-PRIME-COVARIANCE','uniform','Under RH, for every fixed D>0, Z_p=(sqrt(p)e^(−i gamma logp)−1)/sqrt(p−1), primes p<=log^D Y, has centered covariance I+O_D((loglogY)²/logY) in operator norm under the normalized derivative-weighted high tail. Unscaled prime entries have O_D(loglogY/logY) absolute error.','Only covariance, not a growing-dimensional joint law; all-integer unscaled entries also converge uniformly for P=o(logY). No effective onset from Siegel-based source proof.','growing_block_covariance_theorem')
c('THM-PRIME-ARRAY-COMPUTABLE-REMAINDER','remainder','Under RH, a complete certified finite critical-zero list and local disk majorants give |sqrt(logN E_N)−sqrt(C_F)|<=alpha+q sqrt(c_plus)/(1+sqrt(1−q)) and |logN E_N−C2|<=2sqrt(c_plus+A(Y))eta+eta², with all quantities explicitly defined in the cited proof.','All-zero cutoff completeness and multiplicity, disjoint finite windows, actual anchor; B(Y) controls near-function tail while the improved A(Y) controls coefficient tail only. No practical small threshold claimed.','explicit_finite_height_convergence_modulus')
c('THM-EXPLICIT-CRITICAL-DERIVATIVE-TAIL','remainder','Unconditionally sum_(0<gamma<=T,critical)|zeta prime(1/2+i gamma)|²<=260000Tlog^4(4T) for T>=16. The two-sided factorialk2 derivative series tail for Y>=16 is <=6.24e6/Y[H4+4H3+12H2+24H+24]<=2.1e7H4/Y, H=log(4Y).','Only critical-line zeros counted, multiple zeros contribute0; no RH for these bounds. RH only identifies the series with the prescribed-array limit. Explicit HardyZ/Cauchy/Rolle and Gaussian strip mean square proof.','unconditional_effective_tail_bound')
c('CERT-PRIME-DERIVATIVE-HEIGHT100','remainder','A complete count of29positive zeros through100 with simple disjoint line-zero balls yields finite derivative sum in[0.25253801685456458,0.25253801685456460]. The entire critical-line series is in[0.25253801685456458,1.716e8].','Unconditional count/jet/tail certificate;128bitdirector and192bitindependentArbreplays. RH only for interpreting the full series as C2. No large-height list computed.','validated_finite_zeros_plus_effective_tail')
